## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates the ability to translate a compliance feature into a concrete, time-bound cost-benefit analysis suitable for a beginner. It tests how assumptions drive ROI and how to articulate go/no-go criteria.

## Key Concepts

- Cost estimation basics for small features
- ROI calculation and break-even timing
- Risk penalties avoided and adoption uplift
- Simple, testable calculations and trade-offs

## Code Example

```javascript
function breakEvenMonths(laborRatePerHr, weeks, engineers, monthlyOverhead, annualBenefit) {
  const upfront = laborRatePerHr * weeks * engineers * 40;
  const monthlyBenefit = annualBenefit / 12;
  const netMonthlyBenefit = monthlyBenefit - monthlyOverhead;
  if (netMonthlyBenefit <= 0) return Infinity;
  return Math.ceil(upfront / netMonthlyBenefit);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you adjust for ARR vs one-time benefits?
- What metrics would you track after launch to validate forecasts?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to model privacy-preserving analytics, not ML, with real-world trade-offs across storage, compute, energy, and compliance.

## Key Concepts
- Privacy budgets & CRDTs for local aggregation
- Edge-resource constraints and telemetry design
- Compliance costs and regulatory penalties

## Code Example
```javascript
// Simple CRDT-like Grow-Only Counter
class GCounter { constructor() { this.counters = new Map(); }
inc(k, v=1){ this.counters.set(k, Math.max((this.counters.get(k)||0)+v,0)); }
merge(other){ for(const [k,v] of other.counters){ this.counters.set(k, Math.max((this.counters.get(k)||0), v)); } }
value(){ let s=0; for(const v of this.counters.values()) s+=v; return s; }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle CRDT reconciliation when offline and merging after sync?
- What metrics would you track to detect drift in your aggregates and how would you price the analytics feature?

## Why This Is Asked

Assesses designing a privacy-conscious, on-device NLP feature with energy, storage, and regulatory constraints, plus a quantified cost-benefit trade-off.

## Key Concepts

- On-device ML and multilingual support
- Energy budgeting, latency targets, local storage planning
- Privacy budgets, regulatory/compliance costs, opt-in controls
- Staged rollout and metrics for go/no-go decisions

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo inference loop for on-device summarization
function summarize(conversation, model) {
  // assume preloaded model in memory
  const chunk = chunkify(conversation, 512);
  return chunk.map(c => model.infer(c)).join(" ");
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate privacy guarantees during updates?
- How would you measure missed insights vs. privacy budget over time?

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses ability to translate connectivity challenges into a minimal, privacy-conscious on-device flow with cost trade-offs.

## Key Concepts
- Edge batching, offline queues, deduping
- Energy/memory budgeting, latency impact
- Privacy, consent, rollout strategy

## Code Example
```javascript
function batchRequests(requests, maxBatch) {
  const batches = [];
  for (let i = 0; i < requests.length; i += maxBatch) {
    batches.push(requests.slice(i, i + maxBatch));
  }
  return batches;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle failed batches in poor connectivity differently for iOS vs Android?
- What telemetry would you collect to validate break-even without compromising privacy?

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses ability to model edge AI costs with privacy constraints, including memory, energy, latency, and rollout economics.

## Key Concepts
- Edge ML cost modeling
- Latency vs. accuracy trade-offs
- Privacy-by-design and consent flows
- Rollout strategy and maintenance plans

## Code Example
```javascript
// Simple cost model for edge translation + summarization
function estimateCBA({translatorMB, summarizerMB, words, energyPerWord, latencyPerWord}) {
  const energy = words * energyPerWord;
  const memory = translatorMB + summarizerMB;
  const latency = words * latencyPerWord;
  return { energy, memory, latency };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you measure model drift and trigger retraining?
- What metrics define a successful roll-out vs. go/no-go decision?
